                <pb facs="1142" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/336g</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-04">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>55. Department’s telegram to-day regarding Red Cross ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hamburg</hi>. Request Foreign Office to instruct German Consul, New York,
                    to give up <hi rendition="#italic">Hamburg’s</hi> papers so that she may dear.
                    He refuses to give up papers without authority. Report immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
